From 64507e5606b7e75fd8aa84ac29086c6673080766 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:27:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/28] cellSpurs: CellSyncLFQueue push for SPURS LF queues

_cellSpursLFQueueInitialize now lays the line out as RPCS3's
syncLFQueueInitialize does, and _cellSpursLFQueuePushBody ports
_cellSyncLFQueueGetPushPointer/_CompletePushPointer (no event queue),
with the SPURS signal: the waiter id an SPU records in hs1 is
(workload id << 8) | task id, and for a SPURS owner (eaSignal bit 0)
the taskset is that workload's argument in wklInfo1. Every step runs
under the lock-line lock with a coherency notify, so SPU reservations
on the line see it as one atomic store.

ANY2ANY is not implemented anywhere public (RPCS3's "2" variants are
stubs); a queue created ANY2ANY is run as PPU2SPU, which is what a
PPU-producer/SPU-consumer queue (Edge zlib's inflate queue in 3D Dot
Game Heroes) does. An SPU push to it gets CELL_SYNC_ERROR_PERM from the
title's own library.

Verified on that queue with the new SPU_LINE_TRACE (LFQ_TRACE=1 traces
the queue): the SPU reserves (pop1.h4), completes (pop1.h1), inflates,
sets its completion flag, then registers as a waiter for the next push.

cellSpursLFQueueDetachLv2EventQueue added (no event queue attached).
